Feature: Original-owned native static triangle interchange
  Scenario: Every represented proxy has an original-funded identity local placement
    Given the actual native graph context WorldCoordinateSystem axis
    When the original geometry importer authors represented proxies
    Then each proxy ObjectPlacement refers to IfcLocalPlacement
    And PlacementRelTo is unset and RelativePlacement is that actual axis
    And original graph backing admits seven base rows plus five rows per primitive
    And denied and cancelled prefixes retire with the same recipient

  Scenario Outline: A denied original frontier preserves every previously accepted prefix
    Given an original glTF Pack or natural GLB source and its actual parent decoder
    And its next physical frontier requires a positive <axis> demand
    And the original <axis> grant is zero
    When the registered IFC4x3 geometry importer advances
    Then that frontier copies no source byte, typed row or output byte
    And that frontier makes no allocation or observer callback
    And every previously admitted prefix stays in original custody
    And the refusal stays with its original retirement recipient
    Examples:
      | axis |
      | items |
      | copy bytes |
      | capacity bytes |
      | release bytes |
      | depth |

  Scenario: Original natural GLB chunks remain borrowed until typed receiving completes
    Given pinned official Khronos BoxInterleaved source bytes
    When the registered native importer receives static triangles
    Then JSON and BIN are traversed without a joined document or binary mirror
    And vertex values use the authored node matrix without TRS recomposition
    And the IFC graph uses SI metres and Z-up coordinates
    And the output contains 12 triangles with official world bounds
    And any material or non-geometric metadata loss is reported

  Scenario: Natural JSON follows glTF numeric and member rules
    Given integer-valued fields written with decimals or exponents
    And duplicate object keys whose final value is authoritative
    And an optional initial UTF-8 BOM
    When bounded natural receiving completes
    Then static geometry equals the last-key-wins official reference interpretation
    And native Pack record duplicate-field admission remains strict

  Scenario: Accepted work cancellation retains the physical prefix
    Given an original native geometry route with a completed-work cancellation threshold
    When a typed source row or geometry chunk passes that threshold
    Then the accepted row or chunk is included in its physical progress receipt
    And no final artifact is published
    And all source, parser, geometry and partial output owners drain with the same recipient

  Scenario Outline: Static accessor and world-transform topology agree with independent readers
    Given pinned official <sample> source bytes
    When the actual registered natural importer and IFC geometry exporter complete
    Then triangle indices and world coordinates agree with three.js within eight relative epsilon
    And the emitted natural GLB passes the Khronos validator
    And the IFC graph passes the independent IfcOpenShell geometry oracle
    Examples:
      | sample |
      | Triangle |
      | TriangleWithoutIndices |
      | BoxInterleaved |
      | NegativeScaleTest |

  Scenario: Malformed natural binary padding is refused atomically
    Given a GLB whose JSON chunk padding includes a byte other than space
    Or whose BIN padding includes a byte other than zero
    When bounded natural receiving visits the padding
    Then it refuses when visiting the actual original padding byte
    And publishes no target artifact

  Scenario: Unsupported semantics do not masquerade as static geometry
    Given animation, skinning, morph targets, sparse accessors or required extensions
    When the native geometry route reaches the relevant authored source field
    Then it refuses explicitly before publishing an artifact
    And all admitted source and partial geometry owners remain drainable
